<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <%- include('include/head', { title: 'More Work — ASIM 3310', extraCSS: ['generative.css'] }) %>
  <style>
    .gradient-asim { background: linear-gradient(160deg, #d0ecd8 0%, #e8f0d0 50%, #f8f0c8 100%) !important; }
    nav { --nav-bg: rgba(208,236,216,0.95); background: rgba(208,236,216,0.85); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(120,180,130,0.2); }

    /* Lock all content to same container so left edges align */
    .page-hero { max-width: 1280px; }

    .work-content { max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--side); }

    .video-full { max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--side) 1rem; }
    .video-full-wrap {
      width: 100%; border-radius: 16px; overflow: hidden;
      background: #0e0a1a; aspect-ratio: 16/9;
    }
    .video-full-wrap.square { aspect-ratio: 1/1; max-width: 720px; }
    .video-full-wrap video {
      width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain;
      display: block; border-radius: 16px;
    }
    .video-pair { max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--side) 1rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .video-pair .video-full-wrap { aspect-ratio: 1/1; }
    @media (max-width: 700px) { .video-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

    .video-caption {
      margin-top: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.15rem;
      font-style: italic; color: var(--text-light);
    }

    .project-block { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .project-label {
      font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.22em;
      text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-light); margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    .project-body {
      font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.85;
      max-width: 680px; margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    /* tighter dividers */
    .section-divider { margin: 1.2rem 0 1.2rem; }

    .back-nav {
      max-width: 1400px; margin: 2rem auto 0;
      padding: 2rem var(--side) 5rem;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(200,170,100,0.2);
    }
    .back-nav a {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem;
      font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--text-mid);
      text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.2s, gap 0.2s;
    }
    .back-nav a:hover { color: var(--text-dark); gap: 0.9rem; }

    @media (max-width: 600px) { :root { --side: 1.2rem; } }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="gradient-bg gradient-asim"></div>

<%- include('include/header-nav') %>

<div class="page-hero">
  <a href="/portfolio/asim-3310" class="back-link">&#8592; Back to ASIM 3310</a>
  <p class="page-eyebrow">Collection &mdash; Spring 2026</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">More Work</h1>
  <p class="page-desc">A series of smaller scale experiments developed alongside larger installations, focused on testing interaction, generative graphics, sound, and visual storytelling through TouchDesigner.</p>
  <div class="page-tags">
    <span class="tag">TouchDesigner</span>
    <span class="tag">Generative Systems</span>
    <span class="tag">Visual Experiments</span>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="work-content">
  <div class="gallery-divider"></div>
  <div class="project-block">
    <p class="project-label">Project 01</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- 1. Sun Glow -->
<div class="video-full">
  <div class="video-full-wrap">
    <video controls preload="none" poster="/images/asim/sunglowSS.jpg">
      <source src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dijso2iol/video/upload/q_auto/f_auto/v1778280010/sunglow_ogz13c.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    </video>
  </div>
  <p class="video-caption">Sun Glow, 2026, 1280px &times; 720px, TouchDesigner</p>
</div>

<div class="work-content">
  <p class="project-body">Sunglow was created during the early development of Flutter while experimenting with generative visuals for projection mapping onto miniature 3D printed butterflies. Using a custom ramp component in TouchDesigner, I explored different color palettes and soft glowing particle effects to test how light, color, and movement translated onto physical objects.</p>

  <div class="section-divider"></div>
  <div class="project-block">
    <p class="project-label">Project 02</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- 2 & 3: Seaweed + Warped side by side -->
<div class="video-pair">
  <div>
    <div class="video-full-wrap">
      <video controls preload="none" poster="/images/asim/seaweedSS.jpg">
        <source src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dijso2iol/video/upload/q_auto/f_auto/v1778204634/seaweed_xgtncx.mp4" type="video/mp4">
      </video>
    </div>
    <p class="video-caption">Seaweed, 2026, 720px &times; 720px, TouchDesigner</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <div class="video-full-wrap">
      <video controls preload="none" poster="/images/asim/circleSS.jpg">
        <source src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dijso2iol/video/upload/q_auto/f_auto/v1778204636/circle_eyyh37.mp4" type="video/mp4">
      </video>
    </div>
    <p class="video-caption">Warped, 2026, 720px &times; 720px, TouchDesigner</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="work-content">
  <p class="project-body">Seaweed and Warped are experimental TouchDesigner patches created while exploring projection mapped visuals for Flutter. Both pieces focus on layered movement, distortion, and flowing generative forms. Although they were ultimately too visually complex for Flutter’s final direction, they helped shape the project’s evolving visual language.</p>
  <div class="section-divider"></div>
  <div class="project-block">
    <p class="project-label">Project 03</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- 4. Woah...Waves! -->
<div class="video-full">
  <div class="video-full-wrap">
    <video controls preload="none" poster="/images/asim/wavesSS.jpg">
      <source src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dijso2iol/video/upload/q_auto/f_auto/v1778204663/waves_duflvl.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    </video>
  </div>
  <p class="video-caption">Woah...Waves!, 2026, 1280px &times; 720px, TouchDesigner</p>
</div>

<div class="work-content">
  <p class="project-body">Woah...Waves! was my first hand tracking experiment using MediaPipe in TouchDesigner and became an early study for Coloring. The piece combines responsive graphics, layered video textures, and ambient wave and bird sounds controlled through hand gestures. Pinching manipulates the audio cutoff and visuals, while hand rotation switches between different graphics and sound environments.</p>
  <div class="section-divider"></div>
  <div class="project-block">
    <p class="project-label">Project 04</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- 5. Bricks -->
<div class="video-full">
  <div class="video-full-wrap">
    <video controls preload="none" poster="/images/asim/bricksSS.jpg">
      <source src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dijso2iol/video/upload/q_auto/f_auto/v1778204630/bricks_hzb9hq.mp4" type="video/mp4">
    </video>
  </div>
  <p class="video-caption">Bricks, 2026, 1280px &times; , TouchDesigner</p>
</div>

<div class="work-content">
  <p class="project-body">Bricks expands on the interaction systems explored in Woah...Waves! while focusing entirely on visuals generated within TouchDesigner. Using hand tracking and gesture controls, the piece experiments with scale, rotation, block movement, and audio interaction to create a more structured and geometric visual environment.</p>
</div>

